      "title": "Shift Left Is Becoming A System-Level Problem",
      "date": "2026-11-02",
      "source": "SemiEngineering",
      "url": "https://semiengineering.com/shift-left-is-becoming-a-system-level-problem/",
      "summary": "Rise in complexity is pushing engineers to validate hardware, software, and physical constraints earlier in the design flow, but fragmented workflows make that difficult. The post Shift Left Is Becoming A System-Level Problem appeared first on Semiconductor Engineering.",
      "body": "Key Takeaways:\n\nShift left is pushing beyond verification to system-level validation.\n\nFragmented workflows with disconnected tools and models are allowing bugs to escape even though individual components have been verified.\n\nAgentic AI may improve coordination across disciplines, identify bottlenecks, and optimize tool usage, but it cannot replace fundamental processes such as simulation and emulation.\n\nExperts at the Table: Semiconductor Engineering sat down to discuss why shift left is pushing beyond verification to system-level validation, and where AI can and cannot help, with Frank Schirrmeister, executive director of strategy programs and system solutions at Synopsys; Ronen Laviv, vice president of business development and strategic partnerships at Hiveware; Jack Berg, vice president of business development at Silvaco; Ashish Darbari, founder and CEO of Axiomise. What follows are excerpts of that conversation. To view part one of this discussion, click here.\n\nL-R: Silvaco’s Berg",
