      "url": "https://semiengineering.com/putting-ai-to-the-test/",
      "summary": "Who verifies the verifier? This is the age-old question for anyone involved in the verification of semiconductor systems. Who verifies AI? The post Putting AI To The Test appeared first on Semiconductor Engineering.",
      "body": "There are an increasing number of new EDA companies these days, and this is great news. The industry needs some new vitality, new thought leaders, people willing to take risks. The same goes for established companies that cannot go outside their existing comfort zone while meeting next quarter’s financial goals. But sometimes, new startups forget the risks associated with semiconductor design. While they may be able to point to an improvement in time to market, or meeting better performance goals, they fail to understand how small that particular step is in the whole process.\n\nToday, a number of companies want us to believe that AI can do everything. Some point the way to automating design, others to verification, and some even claim it can do both at the same time, from the same source material. No, it can’t. While some of it may be possible in the future, it is far from that point today.\n\nWhat many of them fail to do is show proof. One example, one design, one piece of IP is not proo",
